1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,030
On the night of the storm, nobody could see the summit.

2
00:00:04,639 --> 00:00:05,670
Only white.

3
00:00:06,280 --> 00:00:07,223
Only wind.

4
00:00:08,873 --> 00:00:11,503
Two weeks later, the search was called off.

5
00:00:12,253 --> 00:00:14,443
Helicopters can't fly that high.

6
00:00:15,053 --> 00:00:17,628
And in that weather, people don't survive.

7
00:00:19,278 --> 00:00:23,728
For the whole world, a climber named Ilyas was missing, presumed dead.

8
00:00:24,358 --> 00:00:26,018
But Ilyas was alive.

9
00:00:27,668 --> 00:00:28,878
And he had a number.

10
00:00:29,568 --> 00:00:30,498
Forty-four.

11
00:00:31,188 --> 00:00:37,039
Forty-four days until the weather window, when the winds would drop enough to try to get down alone.

12
00:00:38,689 --> 00:00:41,539
This is the story of those forty-four days.

13
00:00:42,149 --> 00:00:44,767
And of the one thing Ilyas got wrong.

14
00:00:54,817 --> 00:00:56,287
It came out of nowhere.

15
00:00:56,917 --> 00:01:01,327
One moment, the sky above the summit was clear and deep blue.

16
00:01:01,957 --> 00:01:05,348
The next, a wall of cloud swallowed the ridge.

17
00:01:06,998 --> 00:01:10,308
The wind hit at over a hundred kilometers an hour.

18
00:01:10,918 --> 00:01:12,648
Ice needles in the face.

19
00:01:13,258 --> 00:01:15,614
The rope ahead of him vanished into white.

20
00:01:17,264 --> 00:01:19,654
Ilyas did the only thing he could.

21
00:01:20,244 --> 00:01:24,234
He found a ledge below the ridge, dug in, and pitched a small tent.

22
00:01:24,844 --> 00:01:27,831
It was half torn before he even crawled inside.

23
00:01:29,481 --> 00:01:32,071
The ledge sat above eight thousand meters.

24
00:01:32,701 --> 00:01:35,011
Climbers call it the death zone.

25
00:01:35,621 --> 00:01:39,531
The air holds only a third of the oxygen you breathe at sea level.

26
00:01:40,121 --> 00:01:41,611
Every breath burns.

27
00:01:42,221 --> 00:01:44,229
At night, it's minus forty.

28
00:01:45,879 --> 00:01:49,409
Far below, at base camp, his team waited.

29
00:01:50,079 --> 00:01:52,569
They called his name on the radio for days.

30
00:01:53,159 --> 00:01:54,390
Nobody answered.

31
00:01:56,040 --> 00:01:58,190
His radio had died on the first night.

32
00:01:58,800 --> 00:02:00,650
The cold had killed the battery.

33
00:02:01,260 --> 00:02:04,030
All he had left was a satellite tracker.

34
00:02:04,640 --> 00:02:06,750
And it could only do one thing.

35
00:02:07,360 --> 00:02:07,921
Count.

36
00:02:13,171 --> 00:02:15,721
Inside the tent, Ilyas took stock.

37
00:02:16,491 --> 00:02:18,861
A bag of freeze-dried food.

38
00:02:19,471 --> 00:02:22,201
One small gas canister for the stove.

39
00:02:22,891 --> 00:02:23,561
A knife.

40
00:02:24,231 --> 00:02:25,661
A plastic flask.

41
00:02:26,391 --> 00:02:29,157
And a sleeping bag, stiff with frost.

42
00:02:30,807 --> 00:02:32,197
He made two rules.

43
00:02:32,787 --> 00:02:34,997
Rule one: strict rationing.

44
00:02:35,627 --> 00:02:39,617
A handful of food and a few sips of warm water a day.

45
00:02:40,227 --> 00:02:43,818
Every minute the stove burned was fuel he would never get back.

46
00:02:45,468 --> 00:02:48,798
Rule two: never go outside after sunset.

47
00:02:49,508 --> 00:02:53,498
When the sun dropped behind the peaks, the temperature fell like a stone.

48
00:02:54,128 --> 00:02:58,194
Outside, at night, frostbite comes in minutes.

49
00:02:59,844 --> 00:03:04,094
To keep track of time, he scratched a line on the flask with his knife.

50
00:03:04,824 --> 00:03:06,630
One line for every day.

51
00:03:08,280 --> 00:03:08,610
One.

52
00:03:09,260 --> 00:03:09,650
Two.

53
00:03:10,260 --> 00:03:10,790
Seven.

54
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:11,992
Twelve.

55
00:03:17,242 --> 00:03:19,112
The days became the same day.

56
00:03:19,722 --> 00:03:20,632
Melt snow.

57
00:03:21,242 --> 00:03:22,132
Eat a little.

58
00:03:22,802 --> 00:03:23,232
Sleep.

59
00:03:24,022 --> 00:03:25,210
Listen to the wind.

60
00:03:26,860 --> 00:03:29,330
Melting snow was the hardest part.

61
00:03:29,940 --> 00:03:33,250
A whole pot of snow gives you only a cup of water.

62
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:36,092
And every cup costs gas.

63
00:03:37,742 --> 00:03:39,352
And the wind never stopped.

64
00:03:40,162 --> 00:03:45,863
It slammed the tent so hard, it felt like something outside was trying to tear it off the mountain.

65
00:03:47,513 --> 00:03:49,623
Sometimes he heard voices in it.

66
00:03:50,353 --> 00:03:51,123
His mother.

67
00:03:51,733 --> 00:03:54,443
His friends at base camp, calling his name.

68
00:03:55,073 --> 00:03:56,383
He knew they weren't real.

69
00:03:57,033 --> 00:03:59,486
That's what the death zone does to your mind.

70
00:04:01,136 --> 00:04:05,146
One night, he was certain someone was standing outside the tent.

71
00:04:05,756 --> 00:04:07,966
He could see a shadow on the fabric.

72
00:04:08,696 --> 00:04:11,226
He held his breath until sunrise.

73
00:04:11,836 --> 00:04:14,646
In the morning, there were no footprints in the snow.

74
00:04:15,256 --> 00:04:16,419
Only his own.

75
00:04:18,069 --> 00:04:20,979
By day thirty, his body was running on nothing.

76
00:04:21,609 --> 00:04:23,739
He was as thin as a skeleton.

77
00:04:24,349 --> 00:04:26,159
Every breath came with a rattle.

78
00:04:26,789 --> 00:04:29,223
He couldn't feel his fingers anymore.

79
00:04:30,873 --> 00:04:32,483
But his mind stayed sharp.

80
00:04:33,173 --> 00:04:34,363
He kept counting.

81
00:04:34,973 --> 00:04:36,284
He kept the rules.

82
00:04:41,534 --> 00:04:43,124
Then came day forty-one.

83
00:04:43,734 --> 00:04:46,149
The worst storm since the first night.

84
00:04:47,799 --> 00:04:51,709
Around midnight, he heard the sound he had been dreading for weeks.

85
00:04:52,319 --> 00:04:54,009
A long, ripping tear.

86
00:04:54,619 --> 00:04:56,636
The windward wall split open.

87
00:04:58,286 --> 00:04:59,916
The blizzard poured in.

88
00:05:00,506 --> 00:05:02,476
Snow filled the sleeping bag.

89
00:05:03,166 --> 00:05:06,600
The temperature inside dropped to the temperature outside.

90
00:05:08,250 --> 00:05:09,520
He had to fix it.

91
00:05:10,130 --> 00:05:10,860
Right now.

92
00:05:11,470 --> 00:05:17,920
In total darkness, by touch, with fingers he couldn't feel, he pushed a needle through the frozen fabric.

93
00:05:18,610 --> 00:05:19,060
Again.

94
00:05:19,710 --> 00:05:20,537
And again.

95
00:05:22,187 --> 00:05:24,357
Every stitch could cost him a finger.

96
00:05:24,987 --> 00:05:25,737
He knew that.

97
00:05:26,367 --> 00:05:27,761
He kept sewing.

98
00:05:29,411 --> 00:05:31,841
By dawn, the hole was closed.

99
00:05:32,471 --> 00:05:33,521
The tent held.

100
00:05:34,211 --> 00:05:36,866
He had survived the night that should have killed him.

101
00:05:38,516 --> 00:05:40,506
His hands were burning with pain.

102
00:05:41,116 --> 00:05:42,466
And that was good news.

103
00:05:43,096 --> 00:05:44,891
Pain meant they were still alive.

104
00:05:50,141 --> 00:05:53,231
Three days later, he scratched the last line.

105
00:05:53,921 --> 00:05:54,826
Forty-four.

106
00:05:56,476 --> 00:05:57,966
The storm had stopped.

107
00:05:58,596 --> 00:06:01,706
For the first time in six weeks, there was no wind.

108
00:06:02,336 --> 00:06:04,593
Only a ringing, total silence.

109
00:06:06,243 --> 00:06:09,373
He counted the lines on the flask one more time.

110
00:06:10,023 --> 00:06:11,053
Forty-four.

111
00:06:11,683 --> 00:06:15,497
For the first time in six weeks, he let himself smile.

112
00:06:17,147 --> 00:06:21,117
Ilyas cut the frozen zipper with his knife, and looked outside.

113
00:06:22,767 --> 00:06:26,417
The first rays of sun were painting the Himalayas blood red.

114
00:06:27,027 --> 00:06:29,957
An endless ocean of white peaks below him.

115
00:06:30,587 --> 00:06:31,457
He had made it.

116
00:06:32,167 --> 00:06:34,557
Forty-four days in the death zone.

117
00:06:35,167 --> 00:06:35,925
Alive.

118
00:06:41,175 --> 00:06:42,785
Then he looked at the tracker.

119
00:06:43,395 --> 00:06:45,425
He had stopped checking it weeks ago.

120
00:06:46,035 --> 00:06:47,643
He trusted his flask.

121
00:06:49,293 --> 00:06:52,043
The screen said: day fifty-two.

122
00:06:53,693 --> 00:06:54,663
Fifty-two.

123
00:06:55,293 --> 00:06:56,486
Not forty-four.

124
00:06:58,136 --> 00:07:00,926
In the thin air, he had been passing out.

125
00:07:01,556 --> 00:07:02,466
For hours.

126
00:07:03,076 --> 00:07:05,026
Sometimes for whole days.

127
00:07:05,636 --> 00:07:09,359
And on those days, nobody scratched a line on the flask.

128
00:07:11,009 --> 00:07:13,579
Which meant the weather window wasn't about to open.

129
00:07:14,169 --> 00:07:15,839
It had already been open.

130
00:07:16,509 --> 00:07:17,779
For eight days.

131
00:07:18,369 --> 00:07:19,737
And it was closing.

132
00:07:21,387 --> 00:07:25,817
On the horizon, a grey wall of cloud was already rising.

133
00:07:26,427 --> 00:07:27,537
The next storm.

134
00:07:28,127 --> 00:07:29,085
Maybe a bigger one.

135
00:07:30,735 --> 00:07:35,405
Below him lay three thousand meters of ice, cliffs and crevasses.

136
00:07:36,015 --> 00:07:37,673
And he could barely stand.

137
00:07:39,323 --> 00:07:39,953
The food.

138
00:07:40,563 --> 00:07:41,473
The gas.

139
00:07:42,103 --> 00:07:42,873
His strength.

140
00:07:43,583 --> 00:07:45,533
Almost everything was gone.

141
00:07:46,183 --> 00:07:48,053
He had maybe one day left in him.

142
00:07:48,663 --> 00:07:49,666
Maybe less.

143
00:07:51,316 --> 00:07:55,506
Ilyas survived forty-four days at the top of the world.

144
00:07:56,136 --> 00:07:57,486
Or fifty-two.

145
00:07:58,116 --> 00:08:00,187
But the hardest part was still ahead.

146
00:08:01,837 --> 00:08:03,027
Getting down.

147
00:08:03,637 --> 00:08:04,374
Alive.

148
00:08:06,024 --> 00:08:07,034
Could you have survived?

149
00:08:07,704 --> 00:08:10,714
Tell me in the comments how many days you would last.

150
00:08:11,304 --> 00:08:15,074
And if you want to see what happened on the way down, subscribe.

151
00:08:15,744 --> 00:08:17,318
The descent is coming.
